WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.167
The migration runs as six waves: assess,

2
00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:08.037
build the foundation, pilot,
scale, cut over, and decommission.

3
00:00:08.037 --> 00:00:12.390
Each wave's exit gate is the next
one's entry gate, and the durations,

4
00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:17.549
about forty-four weeks for a single
forest, are planning figures, not promises.

5
00:00:17.549 --> 00:00:20.563
The rule that matters
most is about going back.

6
00:00:20.563 --> 00:00:23.616
No wave starts until its
rollback has been rehearsed,

7
00:00:23.616 --> 00:00:27.087
and no rollback depends on
something that same wave retired.

8
00:00:27.087 --> 00:00:30.805
That's why the old automatic
enrollment stays on through the pilot,

9
00:00:30.805 --> 00:00:34.387
and federation stays restorable
for thirty days after cutover.

10
00:00:34.387 --> 00:00:40.013
The decision for the sponsor and CIO: approve
each gate before the next wave starts.

11
00:00:40.013 --> 00:00:42.740
During all of this, both systems are live.
